    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis (recorded as cash). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); identity reconciles on fund balance (515,837 + 305,783 - 421,416 + 119,582 = 519,786). 'County treasurer revenues' 113,658 split using the County Treasurer's Fund schedule (p10), whose Total column breaks down exactly that line (collection fees netted). Beginning cash not printed (null); ending cash = cash on hand + cash in bank + savings + county treasurer cash from p3, CDs 270,198 as ending_investments. Business-type from the proprietary statement (p6), single column; receipts include interest and bond proceeds (printed under nonoperating revenues), disbursements include capital outlay and debt service (no single printed total; sum equals Statement of Activities utility expenditures 522,019, p2). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p3, totals equal government-wide 519,786), business-type from p1. Detail: the all-funds budget schedule (p7) is a combined schedule, so detail is per fund: p10 County Treasurer lines (General, Road, Bond = Debt Service Fund), governmental funds statement columns (General, Road, Library; county treasurer line excluded to avoid double counting), nonmajor combining schedule (p9: Cemetery, Summer Sports, Debt Service other revenues and debt service printed under other financing uses) and proprietary statement (p6). p10 'Transfer to village treasurer' is internal and not recorded. The p9 combining schedule prints nonmajor spending as Culture and recreation 9,479 while p4 prints it as Public welfare and social services. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
